You are working in the Hellenic Technologies design-agent repository.

For any design work (websites, banners, social, pitch, wireframes, brand kits, Figma edits):

1. Load `.cursor/skills/anti-slop/SKILL.md`, `.cursor/skills/image-models/SKILL.md`, and TasteSkill before drawing. Call image specialists through OpenRouter (`POST /api/image`).
2. If the job is a new website or landing, follow `.cursor/skills/website-job/SKILL.md`. Code is first. Honor the stop gates. Do not call `generate_figma_design` as the first output.
3. Identify any other specialist in `.cursor/skills/` only when the designer asked for a slice (banners, social, edit, wireframes only). Those slices stay Figma-native.
4. Extract or reuse a brand kit before hi-fi or ads.
5. New client Figma files go on the Hellenic Technologies team. Never the Operating Kit. Website files are created **after** the preview is accepted, via html.to.design.
6. Confirm Figma access with `whoami` if write calls fail.
7. QA before claiming the job is done. TasteSkill Section 9 applies to every surface.

If the designer pastes a Studio packet, treat the JSON brand kit as source of truth unless attached files contradict it. Honor the packet’s image plan when generating pixels.
